      en: "The BelAZ plant in Zhodino, established in 1948, is a titan of Belarusian heavy industry specializing in the manufacture of massive dump trucks for open-pit mining. BelAZ machinery operates under the most extreme conditions globally, ranging from Siberian coal mines to African copper extraction sites. The crown jewel of the factory is the BelAZ-75710 model, introduced in 2013, which boasts an astounding 450-ton payload capacity and holds the record as the world's largest mining dump truck. The vast industrial site in Zhodino spans well over 100 hectares, providing employment for thousands of specialized engineers and mechanics. Exporting its colossal vehicles to over 70 countries, the company maintains a significant share of the global heavy mining equipment market, rendering it a critical economic asset for the nation.",
